{
  "format": "sfxgen/1",
  "name": "Laser",
  "description": "A shot from a home-computer sound chip with a real filter. A pulse falls from 2.1 kHz to 260 Hz in 140 ms while its width opens from a thin sliver to a square, and the chip's resonant low-pass closes behind it. The player routine retriggers it twice more, quieter each time, 70 ms apart: the cheap echo of the era. Low sample rate leaves metallic aliasing on top.",
